Z||000011||84Bill||06-25-2001||01:08 PM||||Here is one a friend of mine told me<P>There was a fellow named Pat that worked for a university for several years as a janitor, one day while walking the halls he bumped into and old friend of his named Jim. Jim had just recently started working as an instructor in the drama department and was getting together some people for the spring play. Pat was always interested in being in a play and asked if there was maybe something that he could do. Jim said Yeah I need someone for the opening act, it’s a really simple part and there is only one line to say. Pat was very excited at the prospect and asked what the line was. Jim replied “ Hark! Its the cannons!” and Pat repeated the line with perfect inflection. Jim said that’s GREAT! Ok you got the part. Pat was very excited and for the next 3 weeks he would be sweeping the floors or emptying cans of trash all the while proudly saying his lines “Hark! It’s the cannons!<BR>It’s now opening night and the theater goes quiet as the lights go dim, the curtain opens to reveal Pat standing there with his chest out, standing in a very proud and commanding position. Just as he was about to say his line there was a sudden BOOM!! From behind him, Pat does a spinning leap about a foot in the air and says, “What the hell was that!”<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000012||SteveJ||06-25-2001||01:30 PM|||| <BR>       Jake was dying. His wife, Becky, was maintaining a candlelight vigil by his side. She held his fragile hand, tears running down her face. Her praying roused him from his slumber.<BR>        He looked up and his pale lips began to move slightly.<BR>       "My darling Becky," he whispered. "Hush, my love," she said. "Rest. Shhh, don't talk."<BR>        He was insistent.<BR>       "Becky," he said in his tired voice, "I have something I must confess to you." "There's nothing to confess," replied the weeping Becky.<BR>       "Everything's all right, go to sleep."<BR>       "No, no. I must die in peace, Becky. I ... I slept with your sister,  your best friend, her best friend, and your Mother!"<BR>       "I know," Becky whispered softly. "That's why I poisoned you.<BR> ||||reg||1
